			"properties": {
				"asOfDate": {
					"description": "Return the equity summary as of this date, specified as an [ISO 8601 extended format calendar date](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601#Calendar_dates), i.e. 'YYYY-MM-DD'. Defaults to today when omitted.",
					"type": "string"
				},
				"includeCanceled": {
					"description": "When true, canceled securities are included in exercised and settled quantity totals. Canceled securities are always excluded from total, vested, and outstanding quantities. Defaults to false.",
					"type": "boolean"
				},
				"issuerId": {
					"anyOf": [
						{
							"maximum": 9007199254740991,
							"minimum": 0,
							"type": "integer"
						},
						{
							"maxLength": 64,
							"minLength": 1,
							"pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$",
							"type": "string"
						}
					],
					"description": "The identifier of the issuer."
				},
				"stakeholderId": {
					"anyOf": [
						{
							"maximum": 9007199254740991,
							"minimum": 0,
							"type": "integer"
						},
						{
							"maxLength": 64,
							"minLength": 1,
							"pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$",
							"type": "string"
						}
					],
					"description": "The identifier of the stakeholder."
				}
			},
			"required": [
				"issuerId",
				"stakeholderId"
			],
			"type": "object"
		}
	},
	"getStockSplitChanges": {
		"description": "Scope(s): `read_issuer_info`\n\nFor a set of securities you hold and a reference time, reports whether a stock split has occurred for the issuer since that time and, for each affected security, its pre- and post-split quantity and price. Store the returned `asOf` timestamp and send it back as `since` on the next request to reconcile incrementally. Up to 1000 securities may be requested per call; hold more than that and you must page through them in batches.\n\n`splitOccurredSince` can be `true` while `affectedAssets` is empty: a split occurred for the issuer, but none of the securities in your request were affected.",
		"inputSchema": {
			"allOf": [
				{
					"description": "The request to the Get Stock Split Asset Changes endpoint.",
					"properties": {
						"securities": {
							"description": "The securities to check for stock-split-driven changes. At most 1000 securities may be provided per request.",
							"items": {
								"description": "A reference to a specific security held by the caller.",
								"properties": {
									"securityId": {
										"description": "The internal integer identifier of the security, encoded as a decimal string (e.g. \"12345\") — not a UUID.",
										"maxLength": 50,
										"minLength": 1,
										"pattern": "^[0-9]+$",
										"type": "string"
									},
									"securityType": {
										"description": "The kind of security, lowercase on the wire: \"option_grant\" or \"certificate\".",
										"enum": [
											"option_grant",
											"certificate"
										],
										"type": "string"
									}
								},
								"required": [
									"securityType",
									"securityId"
								],
								"title": "v1alpha1StockSplitAssetRef",
								"type": "object"
							},
							"type": "array"
						},
						"since": {
							"description": "The reference time. Only stock splits that occurred after this time are considered. Provide the `asOf` value from a previous response rather than a time from your own clock.",
							"example": {
								"value": "2021-01-01T18:18:00Z"
							},
							"properties": {
								"value": {
									"maxLength": 24,
									"minLength": 20,
									"pattern": "[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}(?:\\.[0-9]{1,3})?Z",
									"type": "string"
								}
							},
							"title": "v1alpha1Iso8601CompleteCalendarDateTime",
							"type": "object"
						}
					},
					"required": [
						"securities",
						"since"
					],
					"title": "IssuersServiceGetStockSplitAssetChangesBody",
					"type": "object"
				}
			],
			"examples": [
				{
					"issuerId": "101",
					"securities": [
						{
							"securityId": "101",
							"securityType": "option_grant"
						}
					],
					"since": {
						"value": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z"
					}
				}
			],
			"properties": {
				"issuerId": {
					"anyOf": [
						{
							"maximum": 9007199254740991,
							"minimum": 0,
							"type": "integer"
						},
						{
							"maxLength": 64,
							"minLength": 1,
							"pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$",
							"type": "string"
						}
					],
					"description": "The identifier of the issuer that owns the securities."
				}
			},
			"required": [
				"issuerId",
				"securities",
				"since"
			],
			"type": "object"
		}
	},
	"initiateSecondarySettlement": {
		"description": "Scope(s): `readwrite_issuer_secondarytransactions`\n\nCreates a secondary transaction in draft and returns it under `secondaryTransaction`, including its `secondaryTransactionId`. Persist that id: every later call is addressed by it.\n\n**A secondary transaction in draft is not a placeholder.** Creating one soft-locks every security in it, so those shares can't be exercised or sold elsewhere in Carta, and it starts the issuer's review. Create a secondary transaction only for a trade you intend to complete. It stays in draft until it settles or is canceled, and the lock is released then. \"Draft\" means the trade is not yet on the cap table. That only changes after you call Finalize Secondary Transaction and the issuer approves the cap-table update.\n\nCarta takes the soft lock itself; there is no lock call for you to make and no lock resource on this API.\n\nThe transfer versus repurchase distinction is carried by `rightOfFirstRefusal.outcome` rather than by separate endpoints: `EXERCISED_BY_COMPANY` drives the repurchase path, and the other two drive the transfer path. `buyerInformation` is required on the transfer path and unused for a repurchase, where the issuer is the counterparty.\n\nThe response returns the full secondary transaction nested under `secondaryTransaction`: the fields you sent, plus Carta's `secondaryTransactionId` and `state`.\n\nBoth outcomes return `200`, so branch on `secondaryTransaction.state`:\n- `PENDING_SETTLEMENT`: certificates only. Move the money, then call Finalize Secondary Transaction.\n- `PENDING_ISSUER_OPTION_COST_REVIEW`: at least one option grant. The issuer must approve the option cost and withholding first. You'll be emailed when it's approved, or you can poll Get Secondary Transaction; then read the tax figures.\n\nSend who decided the right of first refusal, and when, in `rightOfFirstRefusal.decidedByName` and `rightOfFirstRefusal.decidedAt`. The issuer sees both before approving.\n\n**Retrying.** `externalReferenceId` makes this call safe to retry. If you lose the response (a timeout or dropped connection), send the same request again. When a transaction with that `externalReferenceId` already exists, Carta creates nothing, takes no new lock, and answers `409`. When that transaction belongs to this issuer, the `409` carries an `ErrorInfo` detail whose `reason` is `RESOURCE_ALREADY_EXISTS` and whose `metadata.secondaryTransactionId` names it; read it with Get Secondary Transaction for its current state. The `409` does not compare the payloads: the id is that of the transaction the reference first created, whatever this request carried. A `409` with no `secondaryTransactionId` means another issuer's transaction holds the reference; choose another.",
		"inputSchema": {
			"allOf": [
				{
					"description": "A secondary transaction: the sale of an issuer's securities to a buyer, or back to the issuer, recorded under the issuer. You send it on Create Secondary Transaction, and Create, Get and Finalize Secondary Transaction each return it in full, nested under `secondaryTransaction`. `secondaryTransactionId`, `state` and `finalizedAt` are assigned by Carta and are ignored if sent.",
					"example": {
						"buyerInformation": {
							"email": "ada@example.com",
							"firstName": "Ada",
							"lastName": "Lovelace"
						},
						"externalReferenceId": "ABC-2026-0041",
						"pricePerShare": {
							"amount": {
								"value": "10.00"
							},
							"currencyCode": "USD"
						},
						"rightOfFirstRefusal": {
							"decidedAt": "2026-10-20T15:00:00Z",
							"decidedByName": "Jane Doe, General Counsel",
							"outcome": "WAIVED"
						},
						"securities": [
							{
								"quantity": {
									"value": "5000"
								},
								"securityId": "482913",
								"securityType": "option_grant",
								"stockOptionType": "NSO"
							},
							{
								"quantity": {
									"value": "2000"
								},
								"securityId": "482914",
								"securityType": "option_grant",
								"stockOptionType": "ISO"
							}
						]
					},
					"properties": {
						"buyerInformation": {
							"description": "The buyer receiving the securities. Required when `rightOfFirstRefusal.outcome` is `WAIVED` or `EXERCISED_BY_STAKEHOLDER`; omit for `EXERCISED_BY_COMPANY`, where the issuer is the counterparty. Drives stakeholder creation in Carta where the buyer does not already exist.",
							"example": {
								"email": "ada@example.com",
								"firstName": "Ada",
								"lastName": "Lovelace"
							},
							"properties": {
								"email": {
									"description": "The buyer's email address. Also the match key: an existing stakeholder with this email on the issuer is reused rather than duplicated.",
									"example": "ada@example.com",
									"type": "string"
								},
								"entityName": {
									"description": "The buyer's entity name, in lieu of first and last name. Required for a non-individual buyer.",
									"maxLength": 1000,
									"type": "string"
								},
								"firstName": {
									"description": "The buyer's first name. Required for an individual buyer; omit for an entity.",
									"maxLength": 1000,
									"type": "string"
								},
								"lastName": {
									"description": "The buyer's last name. Required for an individual buyer; omit for an entity.",
									"maxLength": 1000,
									"type": "string"
								}
							},
							"required": [
								"email"
							],
							"title": "v1alpha1BuyerInformation",
							"type": "object"
						},
						"externalReferenceId": {
							"description": "Your own reference for this trade, unique within Carta. Stored verbatim and echoed back on every response so you can reconcile against your records. Carta's identifier for the transaction is `secondaryTransactionId`. Resending the same reference on create is how Carta recognises a retry: it answers `409`, naming the transaction the reference already created when that transaction belongs to this issuer.",
							"example": "ABC-2026-0041",
							"maxLength": 255,
							"minLength": 1,
							"type": "string"
						},
						"finalizedAt": {
							"description": "When you finalized the secondary transaction, as an RFC 3339 UTC timestamp; unset until then. Use it to tell whether finalizing is still yours to do: see the `PENDING_SETTLEMENT` state.",
							"example": "2026-10-22T18:30:00Z",
							"format": "date-time",
							"readOnly": true,
							"type": "string"
						},
						"pricePerShare": {
							"description": "The sale price for ONE share, applied to every entry in `securities`. Carta records each line's proceeds as price times quantity and the transaction total as the sum of those lines, so no total is sent. `currencyCode` must be USD for V1; any other value is rejected.",
							"example": {
								"amount": {
									"value": "1000.77"
								},
								"currencyCode": "USD"
							},
							"properties": {
								"amount": {
									"description": "Decimal amount of the specified currency.\nFor example if `currencyCode` is `\"USD\"`, then amount of 1 is one US dollar.",
									"example": {
										"value": "100.57"
									},
									"properties": {
										"value": {
											"description": "A decimal amount represented in string form.\n\nExamples:\n0\n0.0\n1.00\n123.45\n-456.0\n.321\n+1.23456e-3\n1e-05",
											"maxLength": 100,
											"minLength": 1,
											"pattern": "^[\\+\\-]?((0|[1-9][0-9]*)(\\.[0-9]*)?|\\.[0-9]+)([eE][\\+\\-]?[0-9]+)?$",
											"title": "value",
											"type": "string"
										}
									},
									"title": "v1alpha1Decimal",
									"type": "object"
								},
								"currencyCode": {
									"description": "The 3-letter currency code defined in ISO 4217.",
									"example": {
										"value": "USD"
									},
									"properties": {
										"value": {
											"maxLength": 3,
											"minLength": 3,
											"pattern": "[A-Z]{3}",
											"type": "string"
										}
									},
									"title": "v1alpha1Iso4217CurrencyAlphaCode",
									"type": "object"
								}
							},
							"title": "v1alpha1Money",
							"type": "object"
						},
						"rightOfFirstRefusal": {
							"description": "The issuer's right-of-first-refusal decision: its outcome, when it was made and who made it. The outcome carries the transfer versus repurchase distinction. The issuer sees all three before approving the cap-table update.",
							"example": {
								"decidedAt": "2026-10-20T15:00:00Z",
								"decidedByName": "Jane Doe, General Counsel",
								"outcome": "WAIVED"
							},
							"properties": {
								"decidedAt": {
									"description": "When the issuer decided `outcome`, as an RFC 3339 UTC timestamp, returned as you sent it. Must not be in the future.",
									"example": "2026-10-20T15:00:00Z",
									"format": "date-time",
									"type": "string"
								},
								"decidedByName": {
									"description": "Who decided `outcome` on the issuer's behalf, as free text — for example a name and title. Trimmed of leading and trailing whitespace, and a blank value is rejected, so what you read back is the trimmed value.",
									"example": "Jane Doe, General Counsel",
									"maxLength": 255,
									"minLength": 1,
									"type": "string"
								},
								"outcome": {
									"description": "The issuer's right-of-first-refusal outcome. `EXERCISED_BY_COMPANY` drives the repurchase path; `WAIVED` and `EXERCISED_BY_STAKEHOLDER` drive the transfer path.",
									"enum": [
										"WAIVED",
										"EXERCISED_BY_COMPANY",
										"EXERCISED_BY_STAKEHOLDER"
									],
									"title": "v1alpha1RightOfFirstRefusalOutcome",
									"type": "string"
								}
							},
							"required": [
								"outcome",
								"decidedAt",
								"decidedByName"
							],
							"title": "v1alpha1RightOfFirstRefusal",
							"type": "object"
						},
						"secondaryTransactionId": {
							"description": "Carta's identifier for the transaction, assigned when it is created. Persist this; every later call is addressed by it.",
							"example": "6f1e2c34-5a7b-4c8d-9e0f-1a2b3c4d5e6f",
							"readOnly": true,
							"type": "string"
						},
						"securities": {
							"description": "The securities being sold, one entry per security. Every entry must belong to `issuerId`, and no security may appear twice. For an option grant Carta derives the resulting certificate from the grant by cashless exercise. On read, each entry also carries its settlement outcome and — for option grants once the issuer has approved option cost — its tax reference.",
							"items": {
								"description": "One security in a secondary transaction: which security is sold and how many shares, and once settled, its outcome. `newCertificateId`, `effectiveTransferDate` and `taxReference` are assigned by Carta and are ignored if sent.",
								"example": {
									"quantity": {
										"value": "5000"
									},
									"securityId": "482913",
									"securityType": "option_grant",
									"stockOptionType": "NSO"
								},
								"properties": {
									"effectiveTransferDate": {
										"description": "The date the transfer takes effect on the cap table. Populated once the transaction reaches SETTLED.",
										"example": {
